      "id": "R05-abstract",
      "text": "ArticuBot learns to open articulated objects from simulated Franka demonstrations without articulation parameters at deployment. Its weighted displacement model predicts grasping and opening subgoals as learned weighted averages of observed points plus offsets to four gripper landmarks. A subgoal-conditioned diffusion controller uses current object point clouds and end-effector states to generate task actions. Training uses 42.3k trajectories over 322 objects. With 200 training objects and no camera randomization, normalized opening was 0.70 +/- 0.01 with the learned controller versus 0.24 +/- 0.02 with motion planning and IK-based control. One policy opened 20 unseen real objects across Franka and X-Arm setups without real-world training. Deployment requires handles graspable from the fully closed object state and target-object names for segmentation. However, DP3 Transformer Diffusion outperforms weighted displacement with all 322 training objects and no training or test camera randomization.",
